  "source": {
    "title": "Irish News, 18 January 1908, p. 8 (\"Keady\"); also the Frontier Sentinel, 18 January 1908, p. 8 (\"Keady\")",
    "publisher": "Irish News (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every name and figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "\"The triennial election of councillors for the nine seats on the Keady Urban Council\", held on 15 January 1908; Peter M'Knight returning officer. The Irish News says there were nineteen candidates but lists eighteen; twenty-three had been nominated (Northern Whig, 11 January 1908). Labels are the Irish News's, for the elected only (N. Nationalist, A.O.H. Ancient Order of Hibernians, U. Unionist). Smyth (J.P.), Watters, Arthurs, Fegan and O'Neill were old members; the Irish News also calls Lenagh and Comiskey old members, the Frontier Sentinel does not. The Frontier Sentinel prints Comiskey as Patrick Comisky and gives the same figures for the elected."
}
